</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ASANO TOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HITACHI LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKAI KAORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAGUCHI TETSUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANAKA ISAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASANO, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HITACHI, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAI, KAORU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAGUCHI, TETSUO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, ISAO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ASANO TOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKAI KAORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAGUCHI TETSUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANAKA ISAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASANO, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAI, KAORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAGUCHI, TETSUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, ISAO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A liquid penetration test and a Magnaflux test, i.e., non destructive testing, are carried out using image signals from a color video camera that takes images of a test sample, and potential defects including false defects are automatically detected for indication on the screen. True defects are detected from those displayed on the screen. Information on defects can be repeatedly reproduced if the image data are stored in storage means. In a liquid penetration test, chromaticity is determined in various locations on the screen to extract potential defects on the basis of color differences, and true defects are discriminated from false defects by using differentiated color differences. In the liquid penetration test a polarizing filter is used to remove the regular reflection of illumination, while in the Magnaflux test an ultraviolet-rejection filter is attached to the camera to remove noises. Both of the tests can be carried out if a white light source and an ultraviolet source are both provided.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne la conduite d'un essai de pénétration de liquide et d'un test Magnaflux, c'est-à-dire un essai non destructif. On utilise à cet effet les signaux images d'une caméra vidéo couleur qui prend des images d'une éprouvette, puis on détecte automatiquement les défauts potentiels, y-compris les faux défauts, en vue de leur mise en évidence sur l'écran. Les vrais défauts se distinguent parmi ceux qui s'affichent à l'écran. Si on conserve les données d'image dans une mémoire, les informations concernant les défauts peuvent être reproduites de façon répétitive. Dans le cas d'un essai de pénétration de liquide, un calcul de la chromaticité en différents points de l'écran permet d'extraire les défauts potentiels sur la base des différences de couleurs, la discrimination entre faux défauts et vrais défauts se faisant par une différentiation des différences chromatiques. Dans le cas de l'essai de pénétration de liquide, on utilise en outre un filtre polarisant pour éliminer les reflets réguliers d'éclairage, alors que pour l'essai Magnaflux, il suffit d'un filtre anti-UV monté sur la caméra pour éliminer les bruits. Ces deux essais peuvent se faire dès lorsqu'on dispose non seulement d'une source de lumière blanche, mais également d'une source d'UV.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>